+## Start with a short supply trip
+
+Choose **Convoy Follower - Arland Supply Day**, or open its world from the repository root:
+
+```powershell
+npm run workbench:open -- --editor world --project addons/ConvoyFollower/addon.gproj --world Worlds/Showcase/ConvoyFollower_Arland_SupplyDay.ent --authorize-local-test-scripts --execute
+```
+
 Start with one loaded follower, then try two. The scene provides ordinary US drivers, supply trucks, a separate player truck and source/destination storage. Source storage is between the first two trucks; the third requires separate staging for loading. Unit One follows your lead vehicle; Unit Two follows Unit One.
-
-1. Enter character play at **Convoy supply staging - daylight** and close the Game Master editor before interacting.
+
+1. Enter character play at **Convoy supply staging - daylight** and close the Game Master editor before interacting.
 2. On foot at the truck's rear, run the native continuous load action and stop it at the desired amount. For two followers, load both trucks before recruiting. Check matching source/truck changes and stable counts after cancellation.
 3. Use **Join my convoy in closest empty vehicle** on each nearby driver, front to back. Wait for each to occupy the intended truck before recruiting the next, then enter your separate lead truck.
-4. At the destination, stop the lead, open the map and choose **HOLD ALL SEATED**. Wait for **completed: all trucks holding in vehicles**, check the trucks are still, then use **CLOSE MAP** and get out.
+4. At the destination, stop the lead, open the map and choose **HOLD ALL SEATED**. Wait for **completed: all trucks holding in vehicles**, check the trucks are still, then use **CLOSE MAP** and get out.
 5. Use the native continuous unload action at each assigned truck's rear; stop it and verify matching truck/destination count changes. Return to the same lead truck, choose **RESUME ALL** on the map, then **CLOSE MAP** and drive on. The convoy owner can also issue Resume as a settled passenger in that lead truck when someone else drives it.
